WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:04.400
Diggers: a lane battler where you can never rearrange your hand.

2
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.210
In this game, you decide whether you want to go for points or control lanes,

3
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:10.300
with a simple climbing-shedding system.

4
00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:13.410
Each turn, play cards that sit together in your hand

5
00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.760
onto a site between you and a rival.

6
00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:19.140
Beat what's there to take it, and keep the cards you beat as points.

7
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.390
Two players fight over three sites.

8
00:00:21.410 --> 00:00:24.960
With three or four players, you share one site with each neighbor.

9
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:27.080
Let's take a look at the middle of the game.

10
00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.530
My run of 5-6-7 can't beat his three 9s,

11
00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.560
so I poach the 4 off his run and slot it into my hand.

12
00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:39.990
The catch: I have to offer him a card back from anywhere in my hand.

13
00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:44.400
He can decide whether to take it to strengthen his hand, or discard it.

14
00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:48.100
Now my four-card run beats his three 9s.

15
00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:51.670
I take Garden Park and keep his 9s as points.

16
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:53.850
That's the swing the table waits for:

17
00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:56.900
one poached card turns a dead hand into a winner.

18
00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:59.020
Empty your hand to end the season.

19
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.140
Score captures and sites that you control, minus your cards left in hand.

20
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.800
Every season deals you a fresh hand, and a fresh puzzle.

21
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:11.230
Forty-five cards, two to four players, and ten to twenty minutes.

22
00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.760
Diggers. Play it in your browser at darrendon.com,

23
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:17.170
or email me for a prototype.
